<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1424" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aethra</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴθρα</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Oceanus and Tethys</i>, <i>mother of Hyas</i> (in <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				192</span></i> called <i>Pleione</i>), <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 5,
				171</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Daughter of Piltheus and mother</i>
			
			<i>of Theseus</i>, acc. to <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 10,
				131</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 37</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
